        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(install-cli): track mktemp paths and clean up on EXIT",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`scripts/install-cli.sh` created temporary directories during Node user-space\ninstall (and temp files for pnpm workspace rewrites) without tracking them\nfor EXIT cleanup. On failure paths (`fail` after download/shasum errors),\nthose paths leaked under `/tmp`.\n\n`scripts/install.sh` already uses `TMPFILES` + `trap cleanup_tmpfiles EXIT`.\nThis PR matches that contract for install-cli, using caller-side\n`tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; TMPFILES+=(\"$tmp\")` because bash command substitution\ncannot mutate parent-shell arrays.\n\n## Evidence\n\nForced failure through the **real** installer (`OPENCLAW_INSTALL_CLI_SH_NO_RUN=1`\nsource of `scripts/install-cli.sh`, then the installer's own `fail()` after\nregistering a staging temp the same way `install_node` does).\n\n**Before (bare mktemp, no trap):** path still exists after exit 1.\n\n```console\n$ bash before-proof.sh\ncreated=/var/folders/.../T/tmp.5AoDqL1V2v\nexists_before_exit=yes\nBEFORE_RESULT=LEAKED /var/folders/.../T/tmp.5AoDqL1V2v\n```\n\n**After (patched installer fail() path):** EXIT trap removes the registered path.\n\n```console\n$ OPENCLAW_INSTALL_CLI_SH_NO_RUN=1 source ./scripts/install-cli.sh\n$ tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; TMPFILES+=(\"$tmp\"); fail \"proof: forced failure after Node tarball staging temp was created\"\ncreated=/var/folders/.../T/tmp.pUp7NGjwt2\nTMPFILES=/var/folders/.../T/tmp.pUp7NGjwt2\nexists_before_fail=yes\nERROR: proof: forced failure after Node tarball staging temp was created\nAFTER_RESULT=CLEANED /var/folders/.../T/tmp.pUp7NGjwt2\n```\n\nProduction wiring:\n\n```console\n$ rg -n 'TMPFILES|trap cleanup|mktemp' scripts/install-cli.sh | head\n35:TMPFILES=()\n42:trap cleanup_tmpfiles EXIT\n834:  tmp=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\n835:  TMPFILES+=(\"$tmp\")\n1071:    tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n1072:    TMPFILES+=(\"$tmp\")\n\n$ bash -n scripts/install-cli.sh && shellcheck scripts/install-cli.sh\nbash -n OK; shellcheck OK\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `TMPFILES` + `cleanup_tmpfiles` + EXIT trap\n- Register Node install temp dir and pnpm workspace rewrite temp file\n- Avoid `tmp=\"$(helper)\"` helpers that run in a subshell (array never updates)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** install-cli leaked mktemp dirs/files on fail/exit; registration via command-substitution helpers was a no-op under bash.\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS 15, bash 5.3.15, branch `fix/install-cli-tmpfile-cleanup` at current HEAD, shellcheck, real `scripts/install-cli.sh` sourced with `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_CLI_SH_NO_RUN=1`.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n\n  Step 1: source patched installer without running main\n  Step 2: register temp the same way install_node does\n  Step 3: call installer `fail()` to force EXIT cleanup\n  Step 4: assert path is gone; contrast bare mktemp without trap\n\n- **Evidence after fix:** terminal output from the patched installer (above Evidence section): `AFTER_RESULT=CLEANED` after real `fail()`; control `BEFORE_RESULT=LEAKED` without trap.\n- **Observed result after fix:** Forced failure through installer `fail()` removes the registered staging temp. Bare mktemp without the trap still leaks. `bash -n` and shellcheck pass.\n- **What was not tested:** full network Node tarball download fail on CI runners (shasum mismatch after real download).\n\n## Related\n\n- Pattern in `scripts/install.sh` (TMPFILES / trap)\n- ClawSweeper rank-up: terminal output from forced failure in patched installer\n",
        "branch": "fix/install-cli-tmpfile-cleanup",
